          '**Post-Procedure Assessment:**\n- Vital signs stable: BP 132/78, HR 72, SpO2 98%\n- Patient reports feeling well, no pain at injection site\n- No neurological deficits\n- No signs of adverse reaction to medications\n- Injection site clean, no hematoma\n\n**Review of Pre-Procedure Documentation:**\n- Referring physician note (2 months ago): "Right SI joint pain, positive FABER test on right, recommending right SI joint injection"\n- Your clinic note (1 week ago): "Bilateral SI joint tenderness, left greater than right. Positive Gaenslen test left. Positive FABER left. Positive thigh thrust left. Plan: SI joint injection starting with the more symptomatic left side. Will treat right side subsequently if needed."\n- Order entered by your medical assistant: "Right SI joint injection" (defaulted to referring physician\'s laterality rather than your updated clinical assessment)\n- Consent form: "Right SI joint injection" (signed by patient based on the order)\n- Time-out documentation: "Right SI joint injection" (read from the consent form)\n\n**Root Cause Identification:**\n- Discrepancy between your clinical assessment (left) and the order/consent (right) was present before the procedure\n- Multiple points of failure: order entry error, consent discrepancy not caught during pre-procedure review, time-out did not catch the mismatch between the order and the clinician\'s intent\n- You (the proceduralist) injected the side you clinically intended (left) but did not reconcile this with the written order or consent before starting',
