    Section(
      title: 'DOMAIN C: PATIENT MANAGEMENT',
      content:
          '**Immediate Patient Monitoring:**\n- Continue standard post-injection monitoring in recovery area (30 minutes)\n- Assess for any adverse effects from the injection (allergic reaction, vasovagal, neurological changes)\n- The injection itself was performed safely — no additional monitoring required beyond standard protocol\n\n**Correct-Side Injection Rescheduling:**\n- The patient still needs the right SI joint injection per the original treatment plan\n- Schedule the right-sided injection in 2-4 weeks (standard interval for bilateral injections)\n- New consent specifically for the right side with explicit laterality verification\n- Consider the left-sided injection as a therapeutic intervention for her documented left-sided pathology — it may provide clinical benefit and can count toward her treatment course\n\n**System Fix Implementation (Immediate):**\n\n**1. Time-Out Protocol Enhancement:**\n- Implement "active verification" rather than passive reading of the consent form\n- Proceduralist must state independently (without looking at consent): "I am performing [procedure] on the [side]"\n- This is then verified against the consent form by the nurse or technologist\n- Any discrepancy halts the procedure until reconciled\n\n**2. Order Entry Verification:**\n- Implement a required field: "Laterality verified by: [clinician name]" at order entry\n- Clinician must personally verify laterality matches their clinical assessment before order is finalized\n- Order cannot be entered by support staff without clinician co-signature on laterality\n\n**3. Consent Process Improvement:**\n- Consent discussion must include patient\'s own confirmation of the symptomatic side: "Can you point to the side that hurts most?"\n- Marking the intended injection site with indelible marker prior to procedure (already standard for surgical procedures but often omitted for injections)\n\n**4. Pre-Procedure Checklist:**\n- Add a mandatory reconciliation step: compare referral laterality, clinic exam laterality, order laterality, and consent laterality\n- If any discrepancy exists, the procedure cannot proceed until resolved\n\n**Documentation:**\n- Amend the procedure note to accurately reflect what occurred: "Left SI joint injection performed. Note: consent and order specified right SI joint. Discrepancy identified post-procedure. Patient notified. See disclosure note."',
